WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.199
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.499 --> 00:00:08.874
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:14.404
Unit eleven: Climate Action. Today you will talk about conditions with 'unless'.

4
00:00:14.704 --> 00:00:17.159
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.182
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.017 --> 00:00:23.389
Climate policy.

7
00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:28.171
Climate policy means government plans to deal with climate change.

8
00:00:28.783 --> 00:00:31.398
Strong climate policy cuts pollution.

9
00:00:31.983 --> 00:00:35.251
Your turn. Say: Climate policy.

10
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.461
Climate policy.

11
00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:41.450
Carbon tax.

12
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.436
Carbon tax means a tax on pollution from carbon.

13
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:48.351
A carbon tax makes polluters pay.

14
00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.997
Your turn. Say: Carbon tax.

15
00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:56.067
Carbon tax.

16
00:00:56.817 --> 00:00:58.352
Renewable transition.

17
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:03.486
Renewable transition means the change from fossil fuels to clean energy.

18
00:01:04.083 --> 00:01:06.524
The renewable transition needs investment.

19
00:01:07.117 --> 00:01:10.547
Your turn. Say: Renewable transition.

20
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.237
Renewable transition.

21
00:01:15.983 --> 00:01:17.518
International agreement.

22
00:01:18.517 --> 00:01:22.339
International agreement means a deal between many countries.

23
00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.623
The Paris Agreement is an international agreement.

24
00:01:26.217 --> 00:01:29.310
Your turn. Say: International agreement.

25
00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.911
International agreement.

26
00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.081
Climate justice.

27
00:01:37.083 --> 00:01:41.091
Climate justice means fairness for people most hurt by climate change.

28
00:01:41.683 --> 00:01:44.182
Climate justice protects poorer countries.

29
00:01:44.783 --> 00:01:47.830
Your turn. Say: Climate justice.

30
00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:52.225
Climate justice.

31
00:01:52.983 --> 00:01:54.635
Mitigation strategy.

32
00:01:55.650 --> 00:02:00.030
Mitigation strategy means a plan to reduce the causes of climate change.

33
00:02:00.617 --> 00:02:03.348
Planting forests is a mitigation strategy.

34
00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:07.403
Your turn. Say: Mitigation strategy.

35
00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:11.918
Mitigation strategy.

36
00:02:12.683 --> 00:02:14.079
Adaptation measure.

37
00:02:15.083 --> 00:02:18.534
Adaptation measure means an action to live with climate change.

38
00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:22.078
Higher roads are an adaptation measure for floods.

39
00:02:22.683 --> 00:02:25.939
Your turn. Say: Adaptation measure.

40
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.277
Adaptation measure.

41
00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:32.598
Youth climate movement.

42
00:02:33.583 --> 00:02:37.081
Youth climate movement means young people campaigning for the climate.

43
00:02:37.683 --> 00:02:39.938
The youth climate movement is worldwide.

44
00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:44.108
Your turn. Say: Youth climate movement.

45
00:02:46.967 --> 00:02:48.746
Youth climate movement.

46
00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:50.856
Emission reduction.

47
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:55.301
Emission reduction means lowering the gases that warm the planet.

48
00:02:55.917 --> 00:02:58.090
Emission reduction must start now.

49
00:02:58.683 --> 00:03:01.812
Your turn. Say: Emission reduction.

50
00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.248
Emission reduction.

51
00:03:06.983 --> 00:03:08.913
Sustainable infrastructure.

52
00:03:09.917 --> 00:03:14.935
Sustainable infrastructure means roads, energy and buildings that protect nature.

53
00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:18.780
Solar-powered schools are sustainable infrastructure.

54
00:03:19.383 --> 00:03:23.255
Your turn. Say: Sustainable infrastructure.

55
00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.285
Sustainable infrastructure.

56
00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:30.574
Global cooperation.

57
00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:34.802
Global cooperation means countries working together.

58
00:03:35.417 --> 00:03:37.846
Climate change needs global cooperation.

59
00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:42.101
Your turn. Say: Global cooperation.

60
00:03:44.967 --> 00:03:46.595
Global cooperation.

61
00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.477
Environmental accountability.

62
00:03:50.483 --> 00:03:54.967
Environmental accountability means responsibility for harm to nature.

63
00:03:55.583 --> 00:03:58.651
Companies must accept environmental accountability.

64
00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:03.365
Your turn. Say: Environmental accountability.

65
00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.734
Environmental accountability.

66
00:04:09.533 --> 00:04:13.811
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.137
Visal, how urgent is climate change?

68
00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:23.329
Very urgent. Unless we act now, climate change will worsen.

69
00:04:24.417 --> 00:04:25.917
What should governments do?

70
00:04:27.017 --> 00:04:31.594
Unless they cut emissions, floods and droughts will increase.

71
00:04:32.683 --> 00:04:33.859
And young people?

72
00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:40.656
Unless we speak up, leaders won't listen. That's why I joined the youth climate movement.

73
00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.242
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:47.000
Grammar focus: Unless clauses.

75
00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.499
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:49.183 --> 00:04:52.123
Unless we act now, climate change will worsen.

77
00:04:53.017 --> 00:04:55.933
Unless countries cooperate, emissions won't fall.

78
00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:59.418
We will lose forests unless we protect them.

79
00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:06.096
'Unless' means 'if … not'. Use the present simple after 'unless', and don't add another 'not'.

80
00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:11.697
Be careful! Don't say: Unless we don't act now, climate change will worsen.

81
00:05:13.633 --> 00:05:16.631
Say: Unless we act now, climate change will worsen.

82
00:05:16.931 --> 00:05:19.105
'Unless' already means 'if not'.

83
00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:22.703
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:24.861
No Time to Lose.

85
00:05:25.161 --> 00:05:27.683
Climate change is the challenge of our time.

86
00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:31.189
Unless we act now, it will worsen.

87
00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:35.674
Mitigation strategies and adaptation measures are both needed.

88
00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:40.860
A renewable transition and emission reduction need global cooperation.

89
00:05:41.867 --> 00:05:45.434
Unless leaders listen, the youth climate movement will keep growing.

90
00:05:46.533 --> 00:05:50.349
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:51.183 --> 00:05:53.717
Unless we blank now, things will get worse.

92
00:05:54.017 --> 00:05:57.369
A, act. B, don't act. C, will act.

93
00:06:00.933 --> 00:06:02.538
The answer is A: act.

94
00:06:03.683 --> 00:06:06.670
A tax on pollution from carbon is a carbon blank.

95
00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.995
A, tax. B, policy. C, justice.

96
00:06:14.533 --> 00:06:16.649
The answer is A: tax.

97
00:06:17.783 --> 00:06:20.073
Countries working together is global blank.

98
00:06:20.373 --> 00:06:24.781
A, cooperation. B, transition. C, reduction.

99
00:06:28.333 --> 00:06:30.577
The answer is A: cooperation.

100
00:06:31.767 --> 00:06:35.174
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:36.017 --> 00:06:39.096
What climate action do you think is most urgent right now?

102
00:06:47.883 --> 00:06:49.418
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:49.718 --> 00:06:58.954
I think the renewable transition is most urgent. Unless we stop burning coal, temperatures will keep rising, so we need more solar power now.

104
00:06:59.254 --> 00:07:00.951
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:06.116
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and unless clauses.

106
00:07:06.416 --> 00:07:13.027
Today's value is environmental responsibility. Small green actions at home help the whole planet.

107
00:07:13.327 --> 00:07:16.096
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

108
00:07:16.396 --> 00:07:18.735
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

